## Answer Format Rules

| Question type | Format | Example |
|--------------|--------|---------|
| Single number | digits only, no commas/$ | `1234.56` |
| Percentage | number + % | `12.34%` |
| Slope + intercept | [s, i] — keep brackets & comma | `[0.456, -887.123]` |
| Two sub-answers | [a, b] — keep brackets & comma | `[1234567, 12.34%]` |

- Thousand-separator commas are stripped automatically — no need to worry about them.
- Never add units (millions, billions, dollars) inside the answer.
- `round()` uses conventional half-up rounding (0.5 → up), NOT Python banker's rounding.
- Never round intermediate values — only round the final result as specified.
- Use `calculate()` for all arithmetic — never do mental math.

